# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Work with bosonic circuits {#work-with-bosonic-circuits}"
msgstr "Trabajar con circuitos bosónicos {#work-with-bosonic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") expresses a computation directly on **bosonic modes**. It carries no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit count: those enter later, during transpilation, which is how one circuit can be lowered under several encodings and several truncations without being rebuilt.\n"
msgstr "Un [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") expresa un cálculo directamente sobre **modos bosónicos**. No lleva truncamiento, codificación ni número de qubits: estos entran más tarde, durante la transpilación, y así un mismo circuito se puede reducir con varias codificaciones y varios truncamientos sin reconstruirlo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It deliberately exposes a reduced API compared to Qiskit’s [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit), so that qubit gates cannot be applied to a bosonic mode, which would not be a well-defined operation. This guide covers the operations that *are* exposed for assembling larger circuits out of smaller ones.\n"
msgstr "Expone deliberadamente una API reducida en comparación con [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) de Qiskit, de modo que no se puedan aplicar puertas de qubits a un modo bosónico, lo que no sería una operación bien definida. Esta guía trata las operaciones que *sí* se exponen para ensamblar circuitos grandes a partir de otros más pequeños.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why use bosonic circuits {#why-use-bosonic-circuits}"
msgstr "Por qué usar circuitos bosónicos {#why-use-bosonic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the traditional workflow for putting the time evolution of a bosonic Hamiltonian onto a qubit-based architecture:\n"
msgstr "Considera el flujo de trabajo tradicional para llevar la evolución temporal de un hamiltoniano bosónico a una arquitectura basada en qubits:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the bosonic Hamiltonian, for example $H = -\\sum_{ij} b^\\dagger_i b_j$.\n"
msgstr "Define el hamiltoniano bosónico, por ejemplo $H = -\\sum_{ij} b^\\dagger_i b_j$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a truncation and an encoding, and map the Hamiltonian to a qubit operator with them.\n"
msgstr "Elige un truncamiento y una codificación, y mapea con ellos el hamiltoniano a un operador de qubits.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implement the time evolution in qubit space, by Trotterization or another method.\n"
msgstr "Implementa la evolución temporal en el espacio de qubits, mediante trotterización u otro método.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second step comes early, and it makes two decisions that are expensive to take back. The truncation fixes how many levels each mode keeps, and the encoding fixes how many qubits that costs, so both are fixed in the qubit operator before anything else has been done with the circuit. To look at the same physics under another cutoff or another encoding, you map the Hamiltonian again and build the circuit again. What the mapping discards, as well, is the bosonic structure: which terms belong together, and that the terms of a hopping pair are each other’s adjoint.\n"
msgstr "El segundo paso llega pronto y toma dos decisiones que son costosas de deshacer. El truncamiento fija cuántos niveles conserva cada modo, y la codificación fija cuántos qubits cuesta eso, así que ambos quedan fijados en el operador de qubits antes de haber hecho nada más con el circuito. Para ver la misma física con otro corte u otra codificación, hay que volver a mapear el hamiltoniano y volver a construir el circuito. Además, lo que el mapeo descarta es la estructura bosónica: qué términos van juntos, y que los términos de un par de salto son adjuntos entre sí.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") moves those decisions to the end:\n"
msgstr "Un [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") traslada esas decisiones al final:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the bosonic Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Define el hamiltoniano bosónico.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Express the time evolution directly on bosonic modes, with bosonic gates.\n"
msgstr "Expresa la evolución temporal directamente sobre modos bosónicos, con puertas bosónicas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the truncation and the encoding as part of the transpilation.\n"
msgstr "Elige el truncamiento y la codificación como parte de la transpilación.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit describes *what* computation to perform, and transpilation decides *how* to put it on qubits. The same circuit is then lowered at every cutoff and under every encoding, and the grouping of the operator is still there for the passes that can use it. The next sections show how such a circuit is assembled; [Transpile bosonic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) shows it being lowered.\n"
msgstr "El circuito describe *qué* cálculo realizar, y la transpilación decide *cómo* llevarlo a qubits. El mismo circuito se reduce entonces con cada corte y bajo cada codificación, y la agrupación del operador sigue ahí para los pases que puedan aprovecharla. Las secciones siguientes muestran cómo se ensambla un circuito así; [Transpilar circuitos bosónicos](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) muestra cómo se reduce.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generic mode indexing {#generic-mode-indexing}"
msgstr "Indexación genérica de modos {#generic-mode-indexing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators#module-qiskit_bosons.operators \"qiskit_bosons.operators\") module and the circuit share one convention for modes. A mode is only an index that labels a bosonic degree of freedom, and it carries no meaning of its own. You can therefore evolve any operator that implements the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, whatever it represents, and the circuit never needs to know what mode `2` stands for. The same holds for the size of a mode: a circuit has no occupation cutoff, so nothing here says how many levels a mode has.\n"
msgstr "El módulo [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators#module-qiskit_bosons.operators \"qiskit_bosons.operators\") y el circuito comparten una misma convención para los modos. Un modo es solo un índice que etiqueta un grado de libertad bosónico, y no tiene significado propio. Por tanto, puedes evolucionar cualquier operador que implemente el protocolo [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait\"), sea lo que sea lo que represente, y el circuito nunca necesita saber qué significa el modo `2`. Lo mismo vale para el tamaño de un modo: un circuito no tiene corte de ocupación, así que nada aquí indica cuántos niveles tiene un modo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Append gates {#append-gates}"
msgstr "Añadir puertas {#append-gates}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gates are appended onto modes. Only [`BosonicGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-gate#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicGate \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicGate\") instances are accepted:\n"
msgstr "Las puertas se añaden sobre modos. Solo se aceptan instancias de [`BosonicGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-gate#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicGate \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicGate\"):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything else is refused, and the error names the offending type:\n"
msgstr "Cualquier otra cosa se rechaza, y el error nombra el tipo infractor:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compose circuits {#compose-circuits}"
msgstr "Componer circuitos {#compose-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.compose\") places the instructions of one circuit onto another. They are **inlined**, not wrapped into a single gate, so the result is an ordinary circuit that you can keep decomposing and transpiling.\n"
msgstr "[`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.compose\") coloca las instrucciones de un circuito sobre otro. Se **incrustan en línea**, no se envuelven en una única puerta, de modo que el resultado es un circuito ordinario que puedes seguir descomponiendo y transpilando.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A composed BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A composed BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-3.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default a new circuit is returned and both operands are left alone. Pass `inplace=True` to modify the first one instead, and `front=True` to put the operand *before* the existing instructions:\n"
msgstr "De forma predeterminada se devuelve un circuito nuevo y ambos operandos quedan intactos. Pasa `inplace=True` para modificar el primero, y `front=True` para colocar el operando *antes* de las instrucciones existentes:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A narrower circuit can be placed onto a chosen subset of the modes:\n"
msgstr "Un circuito más estrecho se puede colocar sobre un subconjunto elegido de los modos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A narrow-composed BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A narrow-composed BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-5.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only another [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") is accepted as the operand, because Qiskit’s own `compose` would inline qubit gates and bypass the check that `append` enforces.\n"
msgstr "Solo se acepta como operando otro [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\"), porque el `compose` propio de Qiskit incrustaría puertas de qubits y eludiría la comprobación que impone `append`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat a circuit {#repeat-a-circuit}"
msgstr "Repetir un circuito {#repeat-a-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat\") repeats a circuit end to end. The repetitions are **flattened**: the result holds the instructions `reps` times in sequence rather than one gate wrapping the circuit. Therefore, the operation counts scale with `reps`, and `decompose` acts on the repeated body instead of removing one repetition.\n"
msgstr "[`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat\") repite un circuito de extremo a extremo. Las repeticiones se **aplanan**: el resultado contiene las instrucciones `reps` veces en secuencia, en lugar de una puerta que envuelve el circuito. Por tanto, los recuentos de operaciones escalan con `reps`, y `decompose` actúa sobre el cuerpo repetido en lugar de eliminar una repetición.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A repeated BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-6.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A repeated BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-6.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the circuit-level way to Trotterize: evolve for a short time, and repeat. See [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) for the alternative of choosing a product formula on the gate itself, and why the two are different things that happen to share the word “repetitions”.\n"
msgstr "Esta es la forma de trotterizar a nivel de circuito: evolucionar durante un tiempo corto y repetir. Consulta [Sintetizar una puerta de evolución en el espacio bosónico](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) para la alternativa de elegir una fórmula de producto en la propia puerta, y por qué ambas son cosas distintas que casualmente comparten la palabra “repeticiones”.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Separate steps with barriers {#separate-steps-with-barriers}"
msgstr "Separar pasos con barreras {#separate-steps-with-barriers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **barrier** marks a synchronization point that optimization passes do not fuse gates across. [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.barrier\") places one on all modes, or on the modes you name:\n"
msgstr "Una **barrera** marca un punto de sincronización a través del cual los pases de optimización no fusionan puertas. [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.barrier\") coloca una en todos los modos, o en los modos que indiques:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A BosonicCircuit with barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-7.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A BosonicCircuit with barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-7.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`repeat(..., insert_barriers=True)` puts one between consecutive repetitions, and none after the last:\n"
msgstr "`repeat(..., insert_barriers=True)` coloca una entre repeticiones consecutivas, y ninguna después de la última:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A repeated BosonicCircuit with barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A repeated BosonicCircuit with barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-8.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers and the encoding {#barriers-and-the-encoding}"
msgstr "Barreras y codificación {#barriers-and-the-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An encoding needs several qubits per mode, so the register of modes and the register of qubits differ in size, and a layout relates *whole registers*. A mode therefore has no qubits of its own to narrow a barrier to. During the boson-to-qubit synthesis a barrier is mapped onto **every qubit of each register it touched**, which is correct under any layout:\n"
msgstr "Una codificación necesita varios qubits por modo, así que el registro de modos y el registro de qubits difieren en tamaño, y un layout relaciona *registros completos*. Por tanto, un modo no tiene qubits propios a los que restringir una barrera. Durante la síntesis de bosón a qubit, una barrera se mapea a **todos los qubits de cada registro que tocaba**, lo cual es correcto con cualquier layout:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A QuantumCircuit showing the expansion of barrier to cover the entire qubit register.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-9.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A QuantumCircuit showing the expansion of barrier to cover the entire qubit register.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-9.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read out a bosonic circuit {#read-out-a-bosonic-circuit}"
msgstr "Leer el resultado de un circuito bosónico {#read-out-a-bosonic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") has no `measure` or `measure_all`. What a measured bit means depends on the encoding. Under a unary encoding the occupation of a mode is spread over several qubits and has to be read from a pattern of bits, and under a compact one it is a binary number, so a measurement that names a mode would have to know the encoding, which a bosonic circuit deliberately does not. Measure the transpiled [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) instead, and decode the bitstrings with [`LevelEncoding.level_to_bits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits\") and the offsets of the [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") that you lowered with. [Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) does this for a complete model.\n"
msgstr "Un [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") no tiene `measure` ni `measure_all`. Lo que significa un bit medido depende de la codificación. Con una codificación unaria, la ocupación de un modo se reparte entre varios qubits y hay que leerla de un patrón de bits, y con una compacta es un número binario, así que una medición que nombre un modo tendría que conocer la codificación, algo que un circuito bosónico deliberadamente no hace. Mide en su lugar el [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) transpilado, y decodifica las cadenas de bits con [`LevelEncoding.level_to_bits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits\") y los desplazamientos del [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") con el que hiciste la reducción. [Simular la dinámica de Bose-Hubbard con una codificación a elegir](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) hace esto para un modelo completo.\n"

